{"id":"mahabharata-9-002","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":2,"title":"द्वितीयोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 2 · Dhritarashtra's lament","summary":{"en":"The king sends the women away and laments, wishing that he had gone to the forest rather than see this day. He recalls the heroes who stood by Duryodhana and asks Sanjaya for an account of the war.","kn":"ರಾಜ ಸ್ತ್ರೀಯರನ್ನು ಕಳುಹಿಸಿ ವಿಲಪಿಸಿ ಈ ದಿನ ನೋಡುವ ಬದಲು ವನಕ್ಕೆ ಹೋಗಬೇಕಿತ್ತೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನೊಡನೆ ನಿಂತ ವೀರರನ್ನು ನೆನೆದು ಯುದ್ಧದ ವೃತ್ತಾಂತ ಹೇಳಲು ಸಂಜಯನನ್ನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"राजा स्त्रियों को विदा कर विलाप करते हैं कि यह दिन देखने से पहले वन चले जाते तो अच्छा था। वे दुर्योधन के साथ खड़े वीरों को याद करते हैं और संजय से युद्ध का वृत्तान्त माँगते हैं।","te":"రాజు స్త్రీలను పంపి విలపిస్తూ ఈ రోజు చూడకుండా అడవికి వెళ్లి ఉంటే బాగుండేదంటాడు. దుర్యోధనునితో నిలిచిన వీరులను గుర్తు చేసుకుని యుద్ధ వృత్తాంతం చెప్పమని సంజయుని అడుగుతాడు.","ta":"மன்னன் பெண்களை அனுப்பிப் புலம்பி, இந்நாளைக் காணுமுன் காட்டுக்குச் சென்றிருக்கலாம் என்கிறான். துரியோதனனுடன் நின்ற வீரரை நினைத்துப் போரின் செய்தியைக் கூறும்படி சஞ்சயனைக் கேட்கிறான்.","ml":"രാജാവ് സ്ത്രീകളെ പറഞ്ഞയച്ച് വിലപിക്കുന്നു; ഈ ദിവസം കാണുന്നതിനേക്കാൾ കാട്ടിലേക്ക് പോകാമായിരുന്നുവെന്ന് ആഗ്രഹിക്കുന്നു. ദുര്യോധനനോടൊപ്പം നിന്ന വീരന്മാരെ അദ്ദേഹം ഓർക്കുന്നു; യുദ്ധത്തിന്റെ വിവരണം സഞ്ജയനോട് ചോദിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.2; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"शल्यपर्व","titleEn":"Shalya Parva","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"विसृष्टास्वथ नारीषु धृतराष्ट्रोऽम्बिकासुतः ।\nविललाप महाराज दुःखाद्दुःखतरं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the women had been sent away, Dhritarashtra, son of Ambika, lamented, great king, sinking from grief into still deeper grief."}},{"n":2,"text":"सधूममिव निःश्वस्य करौ धुन्वन्पुनः पुनः ।\nविचिन्त्य च महाराज ततो वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sighing as if breathing smoke, wringing his hands again and again and brooding, he then spoke these words, great king."}},{"n":3,"text":"अहो बत महद्दुःखं यदहं पाण्डवान्रणे ।\nक्षेमिणश्चाव्ययांश्चैव त्वत्तः सूत शृणोमि वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Alas, how great is my sorrow, that I hear from you, charioteer, that the Pandavas are safe and unharmed in the battle!\""}},{"n":4,"text":"वज्रसारमयं नूनं हृदयं सुदृढं मम ।\nयच्छ्रुत्वा निहतान्पुत्रान्दीर्यते न सहस्रधा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My heart must be made of the hardest thunderbolt-steel, since it does not split into a thousand pieces on hearing that my sons are slain.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"चिन्तयित्वा वचस्तेषां बालक्रीडां च संजय ।\nअद्य श्रुत्वा हतान्पुत्रान्भृशं मे दीर्यते मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Remembering their words and their childhood games, Sanjaya, my heart is torn badly today, hearing that my sons are slain.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"अन्धत्वाद्यदि तेषां तु न मे रूपनिदर्शनम् ।\nपुत्रस्नेहकृता प्रीतिर्नित्यमेतेषु धारिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Because of my blindness I never saw their faces, yet I always held an affection for them born of a father's love.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"बालभावमतिक्रान्तान्यौवनस्थांश्च तानहम् ।\nमध्यप्राप्तांस्तथा श्रुत्वा हृष्ट आसं तथानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When I heard that they had passed their boyhood, then reached youth, then reached their prime, I was glad, blameless one.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"तानद्य निहताञ्श्रुत्वा हृतैश्वर्यान्हृतौजसः ।\nन लभे वै क्वचिच्छान्तिं पुत्राधिभिरभिप्लुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Now, hearing that they are slain, robbed of their sovereignty and their vigor, I find no peace anywhere, drowned in anguish for my sons.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"एह्येहि पुत्र राजेन्द्र ममानाथस्य सांप्रतम् ।\nत्वया हीनो महाबाहो कां नु यास्याम्यहं गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Come, come, my son, king of kings! I am without protector now. Without you, mighty-armed, what refuge shall I find?\""}},{"n":10,"text":"गतिर्भूत्वा महाराज ज्ञातीनां सुहृदां तथा ।\nअन्धं वृद्धं च मां वीर विहाय क्व नु गच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You were the refuge of your kinsmen and friends, great king; where are you going, hero, leaving me behind, blind and old?\""}},{"n":11,"text":"सा कृपा सा च ते प्रीतिः सा च राजन्सुमानिता ।\nकथं विनिहतः पार्थैः संयुगेष्वपराजितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That kindness of yours, that affection, that great honor you enjoyed, king: how could you be killed by the sons of Pritha, you who were unconquered in battles?\""}},{"n":12,"text":"कथं त्वं पृथिवीपालान्भुक्त्वा तात समागतान् ।\nशेषे विनिहतो भूमौ प्राकृतः कुनृपो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How is it, my son, that you who enjoyed the company of kings now lie on the ground, slain, like some common, wretched ruler?\""}},{"n":13,"text":"को नु मामुत्थितं काल्ये तात तातेति वक्ष्यति ।\nमहाराजेति सततं लोकनाथेति चासकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who will now say to me, when I rise at dawn, 'Father, father', and always 'Great king' and again and again 'Lord of the world'?\""}},{"n":14,"text":"परिष्वज्य च मां कण्ठे स्नेहेनाक्लिन्नलोचनः ।\nअनुशाधीति कौरव्य तत्साधु वद मे वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who will embrace me round the neck, his eyes wet with love, and say, 'Instruct me, Kaurava'? Tell me those good words, my son.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"ननु नामाहमश्रौषं वचनं तव पुत्रक ।\nभूयसी मम पृथ्वीयं यथा पार्थस्य नो तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Did I not hear your words, my son: 'This earth is mine in full measure, and not the son of Pritha's'?\""}},{"n":16,"text":"भगदत्तः कृपः शल्य आवन्त्योऽथ जयद्रथः ।\nभूरिश्रवाः सोमदत्तो महाराजोऽथ बाह्लिकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bhagadatta, Kripa, Shalya, the king of Avanti, Jayadratha, Bhurishravas, Somadatta, Bahlika the great king,\""}},{"n":17,"text":"अश्वत्थामा च भोजश्च मागधश्च महाबलः ।\nबृहद्बलश्च काशीशः शकुनिश्चापि सौबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Ashvatthama, Bhoja, the mighty king of Magadha, Brihadbala, the lord of Kashi, and Shakuni son of Subala,\""}},{"n":18,"text":"म्लेच्छाश्च बहुसाहस्राः शकाश्च यवनैः सह ।\nसुदक्षिणश्च काम्बोजस्त्रिगर्ताधिपतिस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"thousands of Mlecchas, the Shakas with the Yavanas, Sudakshina the Kamboja, and the lord of the Trigartas,\""}},{"n":19,"text":"भीष्मः पितामहश्चैव भारद्वाजोऽथ गौतमः ।\nश्रुतायुश्चाच्युतायुश्च शतायुश्चापि वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Grandfather Bhishma, Drona the Bharadvaja, and Kripa the Gautama, Shrutayu, Achyutayu, and the valiant Shatayu,\""}},{"n":20,"text":"जलसंधोऽथार्श्यशृङ्गी राक्षसश्चाप्यलायुधः ।\nअलंबुसो महाबाहुः सुबाहुश्च महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Jalasandha, the demon Alambusa, Arshyashringi, the demon Alayudha, Alambusa the mighty-armed, and the great charioteer Subahu,\""}},{"n":21,"text":"एते चान्ये च बहवो राजानो राजसत्तम ।\nमदर्थमुद्यताः सर्वे प्राणांस्त्यक्त्वा रणे प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"these and many other kings, best of kings, were all ready to give up their lives in battle for my sake, lord.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"येषां मध्ये स्थितो युद्धे भ्रातृभिः परिवारितः ।\nयोधयिष्याम्यहं पार्थान्पाञ्चालांश्चैव सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Standing among them in battle, surrounded by my brothers, I would have fought the sons of Pritha and all the Panchalas,\""}},{"n":23,"text":"चेदींश्च नृपशार्दूल द्रौपदेयांश्च संयुगे ।\nसात्यकिं कुन्तिभोजं च राक्षसं च घटोत्कचम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"the Chedis, tiger among kings, the sons of Draupadi in battle, Satyaki, Kuntibhoja and the demon Ghatotkacha.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"एकोऽप्येषां महाराज समर्थः संनिवारणे ।\nसमरे पाण्डवेयानां संक्रुद्धो ह्यभिधावताम् ।\nकिं पुनः सहिता वीराः कृतवैराश्च पाण्डवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Even one of these, great king, was able to hold them off when furious and rushing at the Pandavas in battle; how much more all these heroes together, who had made enmity with the Pandavas!\""}},{"n":25,"text":"अथ वा सर्व एवैते पाण्डवस्यानुयायिभिः ।\nयोत्स्यन्ति सह राजेन्द्र हनिष्यन्ति च तान्मृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Or else all of them, king of kings, would fight together with the Pandava's followers and kill them in the fray.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"कर्णस्त्वेको मया सार्धं निहनिष्यति पाण्डवान् ।\nततो नृपतयो वीराः स्थास्यन्ति मम शासने ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Karna alone, with me, will kill the Pandavas; then the kings and heroes will stay under my command.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"यश्च तेषां प्रणेता वै वासुदेवो महाबलः ।\nन स संनह्यते राजन्निति मामब्रवीद्वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And as for their leader, mighty Vasudeva, he says, king, that he will not take up arms; so he told me.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"तस्याहं वदतः सूत बहुशो मम संनिधौ ।\nयुक्तितो ह्यनुपश्यामि निहतान्पाण्डवान्मृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Charioteer, as he spoke these words to me many times in my presence, I truly foresaw by reasoning that the Pandavas would be killed in battle.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"तेषां मध्ये स्थिता यत्र हन्यन्ते मम पुत्रकाः ।\nव्यायच्छमानाः समरे किमन्यद्भागधेयतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But that in the midst of them my sons, striving in battle, are being killed: what else can it be but destiny?\""}},{"n":30,"text":"भीष्मश्च निहतो यत्र लोकनाथः प्रतापवान् ।\nशिखण्डिनं समासाद्य मृगेन्द्र इव जम्बुकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bhishma, the glorious lord of the world, was killed when he met Shikhandi, like a lion by a jackal: what else but destiny?\""}},{"n":31,"text":"द्रोणश्च ब्राह्मणो यत्र सर्वशस्त्रास्त्रपारगः ।\nनिहतः पाण्डवैः संख्ये किमन्यद्भागधेयतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Drona, the Brahmin master of all weapons, was killed by the Pandavas in battle: what else but destiny?\""}},{"n":32,"text":"भूरिश्रवा हतो यत्र सोमदत्तश्च संयुगे ।\nबाह्लीकश्च महाराज किमन्यद्भागधेयतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bhurishravas, Somadatta and Bahlika, great king, were killed in battle: what else but destiny?\""}},{"n":33,"text":"सुदक्षिणो हतो यत्र जलसंधश्च कौरवः ।\nश्रुतायुश्चाच्युतायुश्च किमन्यद्भागधेयतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Sudakshina, Jalasandha the Kaurava, Shrutayu and Achyutayu were killed: what else but destiny?\""}},{"n":34,"text":"बृहद्बलो हतो यत्र मागधश्च महाबलः ।\nआवन्त्यो निहतो यत्र त्रिगर्तश्च जनाधिपः ।\nसंशप्तकाश्च बहवः किमन्यद्भागधेयतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Brihadbala was killed, and the mighty king of Magadha; the king of Avanti was killed and the lord of the Trigartas, and many Samshaptakas: what else but destiny?\""}},{"n":35,"text":"अलंबुसस्तथा राजन्राक्षसश्चाप्यलायुधः ।\nआर्श्यशृङ्गश्च निहतः किमन्यद्भागधेयतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Alambusa, king, and the demon Alayudha, and Arshyashringi were killed: what else but destiny?\""}},{"n":36,"text":"नारायणा हता यत्र गोपाला युद्धदुर्मदाः ।\nम्लेच्छाश्च बहुसाहस्राः किमन्यद्भागधेयतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Narayanas, the battle-mad cowherd warriors, were killed, and thousands of Mlecchas: what else but destiny?\""}},{"n":37,"text":"शकुनिः सौबलो यत्र कैतव्यश्च महाबलः ।\nनिहतः सबलो वीरः किमन्यद्भागधेयतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Shakuni son of Subala and the mighty gambler's son, a hero, were killed with their forces: what else but destiny?\""}},{"n":38,"text":"राजानो राजपुत्राश्च शूराः परिघबाहवः ।\nनिहता बहवो यत्र किमन्यद्भागधेयतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Kings and princes, heroes with arms like iron bars, were killed in great numbers: what else but destiny?\""}},{"n":39,"text":"नानादेशसमावृत्ताः क्षत्रिया यत्र संजय ।\nनिहताः समरे सर्वे किमन्यद्भागधेयतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Kshatriyas gathered from many lands, Sanjaya, were all killed in battle: what else but destiny?\""}},{"n":40,"text":"पुत्राश्च मे विनिहताः पौत्राश्चैव महाबलाः ।\nवयस्या भ्रातरश्चैव किमन्यद्भागधेयतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My sons were killed and my mighty grandsons, my friends and my brothers: what else but destiny?\""}},{"n":41,"text":"भागधेयसमायुक्तो ध्रुवमुत्पद्यते नरः ।\nयश्च भाग्यसमायुक्तः स शुभं प्राप्नुयान्नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A man is surely born bound to his fortune, and he who has good fortune obtains what is good.\""}},{"n":42,"text":"अहं वियुक्तः स्वैर्भाग्यैः पुत्रैश्चैवेह संजय ।\nकथमद्य भविष्यामि वृद्धः शत्रुवशं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Sanjaya, I am cut off from my own good fortune and from my sons; how shall I live now, old, fallen under my enemies' power?\""}},{"n":43,"text":"नान्यदत्र परं मन्ये वनवासादृते प्रभो ।\nसोऽहं वनं गमिष्यामि निर्बन्धुर्ज्ञातिसंक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I see nothing better for me here, lord, than to live in the forest. Without kin, with my family destroyed, I shall go to the forest.\""}},{"n":44,"text":"न हि मेऽन्यद्भवेच्छ्रेयो वनाभ्युपगमादृते ।\nइमामवस्थां प्राप्तस्य लूनपक्षस्य संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For me, Sanjaya, in this state, with my wings clipped, there can be nothing better than going to the forest.\""}},{"n":45,"text":"दुर्योधनो हतो यत्र शल्यश्च निहतो युधि ।\nदुःशासनो विशस्तश्च विकर्णश्च महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Where Duryodhana is killed, and Shalya slain in battle, Duhshasana butchered and mighty Vikarna,\""}},{"n":46,"text":"कथं हि भीमसेनस्य श्रोष्येऽहं शब्दमुत्तमम् ।\nएकेन समरे येन हतं पुत्रशतं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"how shall I bear to hear the great roar of Bhimasena, who alone in battle killed my hundred sons?\""}},{"n":47,"text":"असकृद्वदतस्तस्य दुर्योधनवधेन च ।\nदुःखशोकाभिसंतप्तो न श्रोष्ये परुषा गिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tormented by grief at Duryodhana's death, I shall not be able to hear his harsh words as he speaks them again and again.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"एवं स शोकसंतप्तः पार्थिवो हतबान्धवः ।\nमुहुर्मुहुर्मुह्यमानः पुत्राधिभिरभिप्लुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus the king, burning with grief, his kinsmen slain, repeatedly fainting, flooded with anguish for his sons,"}},{"n":49,"text":"विलप्य सुचिरं कालं धृतराष्ट्रोऽम्बिकासुतः ।\nदीर्घमुष्णं च निःश्वस्य चिन्तयित्वा पराभवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"after lamenting for a very long time, Dhritarashtra son of Ambika, sighing long and hot and brooding over the defeat,"}},{"n":50,"text":"दुःखेन महता राजा संतप्तो भरतर्षभ ।\nपुनर्गावल्गणिं सूतं पर्यपृच्छद्यथातथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"scorched by great sorrow, best of Bharatas, again questioned the charioteer, son of Gavalgana, as it truly happened."}},{"n":51,"text":"भीष्मद्रोणौ हतौ श्रुत्वा सूतपुत्रं च पातितम् ।\nसेनापतिं प्रणेतारं किमकुर्वत मामकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When you heard that Bhishma and Drona were slain and the charioteer's son felled, what did my people do about a commander and leader?\""}},{"n":52,"text":"यं यं सेनाप्रणेतारं युधि कुर्वन्ति मामकाः ।\nअचिरेणैव कालेन तं तं निघ्नन्ति पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Whomever my people set as leader of the army in battle, the Pandavas kill him in no time.\""}},{"n":53,"text":"रणमूर्ध्नि हतो भीष्मः पश्यतां वः किरीटिना ।\nएवमेव हतो द्रोणः सर्वेषामेव पश्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bhishma was killed at the head of the battle by Arjuna while you all watched; Drona likewise, as all of you looked on.\""}},{"n":54,"text":"एवमेव हतः कर्णः सूतपुत्रः प्रतापवान् ।\nस राजकानां सर्वेषां पश्यतां वः किरीटिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In the same way the mighty son of the charioteer, Karna, was killed by Arjuna while all the kings looked on.\""}},{"n":55,"text":"पूर्वमेवाहमुक्तो वै विदुरेण महात्मना ।\nदुर्योधनापराधेन प्रजेयं विनशिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Great-souled Vidura told me long ago that these people would be destroyed because of Duryodhana's wrong.\""}},{"n":56,"text":"केचिन्न सम्यक्पश्यन्ति मूढाः सम्यक्तथापरे ।\nतदिदं मम मूढस्य तथाभूतं वचः स्म ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Some do not see rightly, others are deluded; and so my own words, deluded as I was, turned out just so.\""}},{"n":57,"text":"यदब्रवीन्मे धर्मात्मा विदुरो दीर्घदर्शिवान् ।\nतत्तथा समनुप्राप्तं वचनं सत्यवादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What the righteous and far-seeing Vidura told me has come to pass exactly as he, the speaker of truth, said.\""}},{"n":58,"text":"दैवोपहतचित्तेन यन्मयापकृतं पुरा ।\nअनयस्य फलं तस्य ब्रूहि गावल्गणे पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Sanjaya, tell me again the fruit of the wrong that I did long ago, my mind struck by fate.\""}},{"n":59,"text":"को वा मुखमनीकानामासीत्कर्णे निपातिते ।\nअर्जुनं वासुदेवं च को वा प्रत्युद्ययौ रथी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who was at the head of the divisions when Karna was felled? And what charioteer went out against Arjuna and Vasudeva?\""}},{"n":60,"text":"केऽरक्षन्दक्षिणं चक्रं मद्रराजस्य संयुगे ।\nवामं च योद्धुकामस्य के वा वीरस्य पृष्ठतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who guarded the right wheel of the king of Madras in the battle, and the left as he longed to fight, and who stood behind that hero?\""}},{"n":61,"text":"कथं च वः समेतानां मद्रराजो महाबलः ।\nनिहतः पाण्डवैः संख्ये पुत्रो वा मम संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How was the mighty king of Madras killed in battle by the Pandavas while all of you were assembled? And how was my son?\""}},{"n":62,"text":"ब्रूहि सर्वं यथातत्त्वं भरतानां महाक्षयम् ।\nयथा च निहतः संख्ये पुत्रो दुर्योधनो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tell me everything truly: the great destruction of the Bharatas, and how my son Duryodhana was killed in battle.\""}},{"n":63,"text":"पाञ्चालाश्च यथा सर्वे निहताः सपदानुगाः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नः शिखण्डी च द्रौपद्याः पञ्च चात्मजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tell me how all the Panchalas were killed with their followers, Dhrishtadyumna, Shikhandi and Draupadi's five sons,\""}},{"n":64,"text":"पाण्डवाश्च यथा मुक्तास्तथोभौ सात्वतौ युधि ।\nकृपश्च कृतवर्मा च भारद्वाजस्य चात्मजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"how the Pandavas escaped, and the two Satvatas in battle, and Kripa, Kritavarma and Bharadvaja's son.\""}},{"n":65,"text":"यद्यथा यादृशं चैव युद्धं वृत्तं च सांप्रतम् ।\nअखिलं श्रोतुमिच्छामि कुशलो ह्यसि संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Whatever the war was like and however it went, I wish to hear it all, Sanjaya, for you are skilled.\""}}]}]}